{
  "dom_id": "step-q147386",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "A fitness center has $1600$ members, $480$ of which play tennis. If the center randomly samples $60$ members, find a normal approximation for the probability that more than $24$ members in the sample play tennis. You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ are given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9418\\,$ | $\\,0.9429\\,$ | $\\,0.9441\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9525\\,$ | $\\,0.9535\\,$ | $\\,0.9545\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9616\\,$ | $\\,0.9625\\,$ | $\\,0.9633\\,$ |",
